Testing tab -> Playwright -> Tools ribbon at the bottom
This contains tools to create code automatically.

When we have ran a test and still have a page open, we can click "Pick Locator" and hover over elements of a page
This will allow us to see locators of specific elements.
When we click one of the elements we want to locate, the selector will appear near the console in VSC.

We can also generate a whole test. To do this all we have to do is we click:
Record New
A new spec file will appear and a new browser window will appear. All steps we perform will be recorded
Like accessing a specific url, clicking buttons and inserting text.
Afterwards we have to review the code - locators and steps taken.

The third option is:
Record at cursor
When we have part of a test already written and want to continue working on it, we run it to have the browser open.
When it fininshes running, we go back to our test and plance the cursor where we want the rest of the test.
Then we press record at cursor. We are taken back to the browser and can continue with our steps that will be recorded for us.
Again, we have to modify the test we have to make it cleaner.